# Stores

## Purpose

Define the persistence contract so watchers can save and the `ApiController` can read without
knowing which backend is in use.

## Why it exists

The dashboard/API talk to ONE `Store` interface. Swapping SQLite for another backend must be a
drop-in. The default store is also queued for throughput, so the read/write contract and the
queuing behavior must stay stable.

## The Store contract

Extend the abstract [store.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/abstracts/store.ts). Abstract members you
MUST implement: `initialize()`, `save(entry)`, `getAllRequests()`, `getAllQueries()`,
`getAllCacheEntries()`, `allByRequestId()`, `find()`, `truncate()`, `paginate<T>()`, `count()`.

Provided (override only if the backend supports them): `getAllExceptions()` and
`getAllEmails()` default to `defaultMinimalPaginate()` (empty page). Helpers `stringifyData()`
and `defaultMinimalPaginate()` are provided — reuse them.

- `save(entry)` accepts `{ id?, data, minimal_data?, type, timestamp?, requestId? }` and must
  tolerate a missing `id`/`timestamp` (generate a UUID / use `nowISO()`), mirroring
  [better_sqlite.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/stores/better_sqlite.ts).
- List reads use `minimal_data`; detail reads (`find`, `getAllQueries`) use full `data`. The
  `includeFullData` flag + `getSelectedColumns()` implement this split — preserve it.
- `paginate<T>()` returns `Paginator<T>` (`{ meta: { total, lastPage, currentPage }, data }`).

## Default store: composition, not inheritance

The shipped store is composed with the `compose()` helper
([compose.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/compose.ts)):

```typescript
// stores/queued_sqlite.ts
export default class QueuedSqliteStore extends compose(BetterSqliteStore, QueuedStore) {}
```

- [better_sqlite.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/stores/better_sqlite.ts): `libsql`-backed table
  `lens_entries`, WAL mode, indexes on `(id, type)` and `lens_entry_id`, pagination, and
  size-based pruning gated by `dbMaxSizeGb`/`dbPruneSizeGb`.
- [queued_store.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/mixins/queued_store.ts): a class mixin that buffers
  `save()` into a `Denque` queue and flushes batches on an interval; registers `SIGINT`/
  `SIGTERM` to drain then exit. Tunables come from `QueuedStoreConfig`
  ([types/index.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/types/index.ts)): `batchSize`, `processIntervalMs`,
  `warnThreshold`, `preallocate`, `dbMaxSizeGb`, `dbPruneSizeGb`.

Write new cross-cutting store behavior (batching, retry, metrics) as a mixin and `compose()` it
— do not fork `BetterSqliteStore`.

## Wiring

- `Lens.getStore()` returns the configured store or lazily builds the default
  `QueuedSqliteStore` ([lens.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/core/lens.ts)).
- A custom store is injected via `Lens.setStore(new MyStore(...))` before `Lens.start()`.
- Export it from [stores/index.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/stores/index.ts).

## When to create a store

Only for a new persistence backend (Postgres, Redis, remote API, etc.). Implement the full
abstract surface, keep the `minimal_data`/`data` split and `Paginator` shape, call
`initialize()` before use, and clean up resources on shutdown. Do not create a store for a
tweak that belongs in `QueuedStoreConfig` or a mixin.

## Security & safety

- Never persist secrets/PII. Redaction happens in the watcher BEFORE `save()`
  (`RequestWatcher.hideSensitive`) — a store must not undo it or log raw payloads.
- Never `console.log` entry contents; only operational errors (as
  [queued_store.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/mixins/queued_store.ts) does).
- Keep writes non-blocking to the host app (queue + batch); a slow store must not stall
  request handling.

## AI must never

- Make a watcher or adapter talk to a concrete store — everything goes through `getStore()`.
- Change the `save()` entry shape or the `Paginator`/`ApiResponse` shapes without a `major`
  changeset (the dashboard depends on them).
- Duplicate `BetterSqliteStore` to add behavior that should be a `compose()` mixin.
